From 974d21dca419c85f286b2d3a897be627b89d8d31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 16:09:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports: wire ReloadVirtualKey into tenant VK create +
 delete

A new tenant VK created via POST /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/
virtual-keys lived in the configstore but the governance plugin's
in-memory request-path store never saw it.  Every /v1 call against
the freshly-minted VK 401'd with virtual_key_not_found until the
process restarted (which forces a full governance-store reload).

The legacy single-tenant createVirtualKey handler calls
h.governanceManager.ReloadVirtualKey(ctx, vk.ID) after persisting
to close exactly this gap; mirror that in the tenant handler.

Add a narrow VKGovernanceReloader interface (ReloadVirtualKey +
RemoveVirtualKey) so tests can stub it and the handler doesn't
take the whole ServerCallbacks surface area as a dependency.
BifrostHTTPServer already implements both methods, so the wiring
in server.go is one extra argument.

Same hook on the delete path so a VK delete is immediately
request-path-invalid (instead of waiting on the resolver TTL).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
